b-methodology walkthrough — worked case (no CLI by design)
Date: 2026-10-09 · Tool versions: n/a (planning exercise) · Environment: local authoring
Fictional engagement: Harborlight Books loyalty portal (invented; no real system involved).
RoE referenced from b-authorization-scope (not rewritten).

Step 1 — Threat model (1 page): assets ranked — loyalty-point balances (fraud
  impact) > customer PII (breach-notification impact) > admin functions
  (integrity impact); attacker per asset named (fraudster / data thief /
  disgruntled insider). Decides testing-time allocation. DONE.

Step 2 — Recon plan + passive notes: passive items listed (portal pages/JS,
  certificate transparency, archived pages) each with scope status; candidate
  list separated (staging hostname, third-party analytics -> "not in scope,
  amendment required"); active-recon boundary written (DNS vs in-scope names,
  connecting to in-scope ports only). Passive/active split explicit. DONE.

Step 3 — Enumeration inventory: table asset -> endpoints -> parameters ->
  technologies (to confirm) -> WSTG categories. Example row:
  api.harborlight-books.example/v2 -> /points/balance, /points/transfer ->
  account_id, amount -> WSTG-ATHZ, WSTG-BUSL. Every row traces to an in-scope
  asset; candidates kept separate. DONE.

Step 4 — Exploitation proof template: title, WSTG test ID, exact reproduction
  requests, observed vs expected, business impact, remediation direction.
  Filled once with hypothetical WSTG-ATHZ-04 balance-read. Template requires a
  test ID and business impact before any proof is accepted. DONE.

Step 5 — Post-exploitation impact paragraph: business terms (fraudulent
  redemption, notification obligations, trust loss); explicitly states what was
  NOT found (no payment-card exposure in the hypothetical). No tooling, no
  further access. DONE.

Step 6 — Report outline: executive summary, scope+methodology (RoE ref, PTES
  phases, WSTG coverage note), findings ordered by business impact, remediation
  roadmap, appendix with scope-compliance log (tested / excluded / window).
  DONE.

Step 7 — Self-review: all six artifacts trace to the RoE; recon split shown;
  inventory rows carry WSTG categories; proof template requires test ID +
  impact; outline includes scope-compliance log. Filed as one engagement plan.

